# Settings for host/watch.sh on the production host (#303). Copy to
# host/watch.env, which is gitignored: a ping URL is a secret, since anyone
# who has it can report the check up or down. Both URLs are required, and a
# run fails until both are set. docs/monitoring.md, "Install", says where
# they come from.

# The "production" check: host state and the backup. Period 5 min, grace 10.
# WATCH_PING_URL=https://hc-ping.com/<uuid>

# The "errors" check: unhandled 500s and repeated Notion or Claude failures.
# Period 1 day, grace 1 day, so only an explicit /fail sets it down.
# WATCH_ERRORS_PING_URL=https://hc-ping.com/<uuid>

# Where the collected logs, the cursors and the watcher's own state go.
# WATCH_LOG_DIR=$HOME/Library/Logs/planning-hub
